{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1244616-spells-that-affect-wisdom-in-game-explanation-of-why-they-re-impossible","id":1244616,"title":"Spells that affect Wisdom, in-game explanation of why they're impossible","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-10T14:11:36-07:00","id":1244616,"title":"Spells that affect Wisdom, in-game explanation of why they're impossible","content":"Would you tolerate a spell that modifies a character's Wisdom score for its duration?<br /> <br /> If no, can you provide the outline of an <u>in-game</u> explanation about why it's not possible, i.e. how one mage might explain to another mage why it's not possible to use magic to improve her judgement regarding the proper use of magic?<br /> <br /> Also if you have thoughts or experiences regarding how mages discuss Wisdom with one another in general I'll welcome those too. The rules for Wisdom are pretty simple; do mages in your games understand these rules explicitly or is the reason why some mages are better able to resist paradox than others when casting ambitious spells a mystery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T14:31:54-07:00","id":1244621,"title":"","content":"My take; Wisdom only looks like a single, discrete phenomenon, but it\u2019s actually all the continuous feedback loop between a mage\u2019s magic and their surroundings, a microcosm reflecting the macrocosm of relationship between the Supernal and the Fallen. And because it\u2019s symbolically a constantly shifting thing (with 10 dots of it being an abstraction), a spell to affect it would also need to be... Dynamic. Ie. Archmastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T14:44:53-07:00","id":1244625,"title":"","content":"Well I know I'm sold. What a wonderful explanation!<br /> <br /> One thing I'd add is that a component of wisdom is knowing what problems to solve with magic and which ones not to. Solving that with magic would be a contradiction.<br /> <br /> Sounds like gulmoth territory! What fearsome tithe does it hold for the boon of &quot;wisdom&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T14:58:32-07:00","id":1244630,"title":"","content":"Wisdom is a property of the soul and while mages can rip souls out of people, bind them into jars and sacrifice them, they can't actually change a soul in any great way (at least that was my assumption).<br /> <br /> In 1e I think it was pretty explicitly Archmastery territory, entities and excission, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T14:59:38-07:00","id":1244631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1244616-spells-that-affect-wisdom-in-game-explanation-of-why-they-re-impossible?p=1244621#post1244621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take; Wisdom only looks like a single, discrete phenomenon, but it\u2019s actually all the continuous feedback loop between a mage\u2019s magic and their surroundings, a microcosm reflecting the macrocosm of relationship between the Supernal and the Fallen. And because it\u2019s symbolically a constantly shifting thing (with 10 dots of it being an abstraction), a spell to affect it would also need to be... Dynamic. Ie. Archmastery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe I can state it as, &quot;What is Wise depends on context, my friend. It's reactive, mutable -- there are no absolute rules. It's not like throwing a punch or giving a speech, something you can refine through practicing known techniques. You only know what is Wise in a situation when you experience the situation, and what is Wise for you might not be Wise for another. Only an Archmage could magically enhance that kind of personal, dynamic understanding.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T15:02:21-07:00","id":1244632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1244616-spells-that-affect-wisdom-in-game-explanation-of-why-they-re-impossible?p=1244630#post1244630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wisdom is a property of the soul and while mages can rip souls out of people, bind them into jars and sacrifice them, they can't actually change a soul in any great way (at least that was my assumption).<br /> <br /> In 1e I think it was pretty explicitly Archmastery territory, entities and excission, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm afraid if I used this explanation then I'd next have to explain why stealing another's soul doesn't steal their Wisdom rating. I'm trying to close a can of worms rather than open more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T15:05:40-07:00","id":1244633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1244616-spells-that-affect-wisdom-in-game-explanation-of-why-they-re-impossible?p=1244631#post1244631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe I can state it as, &amp;quot;What is Wise depends on context, my friend. It's reactive, mutable -- there are no absolute rules. It's not like throwing a punch or giving a speech, something you can refine through practicing known techniques. You only know what is Wise in a situation when you experience the situation, and what is Wise for you might not be Wise for another. Only an Archmage could magically enhance that kind of personal, dynamic understanding.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sounds like what a mentor would say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T15:16:37-07:00","id":1244635,"title":"","content":"Wisdom has a Supernal symbol, Orders express a fractal view of it in their doctrine the same way there\u2019s a Supernal Chair and many different kinds of chairs in the Fallen. Mages express Wisdom too as even further individuate reflections of Wisdom. Wisdom can be observed via the contortions placed on the jelly soul by the individual (Which springs back into default shape if removed), but otherwise doesn\u2019t really interact with the arcana which is why there isn\u2019t any magic to improve it. It hints at the fact that the Supernal is greater than the arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T15:18:16-07:00","id":1244636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1244616-spells-that-affect-wisdom-in-game-explanation-of-why-they-re-impossible?p=1244632#post1244632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid if I used this explanation then I'd next have to explain why stealing another's soul doesn't steal their Wisdom rating. I'm trying to close a can of worms rather than open more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you could replace 'soul' with 'gnosis' in that explanation. Sophia and Gnosis could be two aspects of the same thing: the Gnosis is the strength of connection to the Supernal, whilst Sophia is the stability of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T18:39:25-07:00","id":1244690,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, there are some spells that target the soul that can cause temporary Wisdom loss, mostly from the Death Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Increasing Wisdom via magic is a completely different beast. As mentioned before, one would require an Archmaster of Death to heal the soul or create a new one, even if a very potent Quintessence was needed. It can also be accomplished via archmastery of Mind, by re-engineering the relationship between mind (thought, action, worldview, intent, etc) and soul into a new system, which may or may not be a good way to break this possible chain the Exarchs placed (as a SIlver Ladder Exemplar would probably say). Another option would be to work on the principle that the soul is composed of the subtle arcana, so you should be able to make manipulate it by mastering them. But doing that requires you to believe in and explore knowledge about the Watchtower of the Soul, which is part of the Tremere dogma, and any mage who cares enough to research Wisdom would probably discredit the opinions of Reapers. Not only that, but attaining mastery of the 5 arcana would require Gnosis 6, and at that point reaching the point of casting Dynamics for Death is much more efficient. Last option would be to find someone who actually had Imperial level command over souls and barter a deal, such as finding Atum in the Underworld or Astral (2 shades of the same Truth, not necessarily equal in power) or the Aeon Typhon, but this could potentially backfire horribly.<br /> <br /> As to why soul loss does not affect Wisdom, its because its effects reflect on the soul, but its nature is Supernal. Think of magic like water, Gnosis determines how that water will be used, Wisdom is the complex system of pipes that transport it from the Supernal to the Fallen. Then it arrives at the soul, which is like an AI that follows the blueprint created by Gnosis and builds the infrastructure to execute the program. But when an act of hubris is commited, it strains or sometimes damages the pipes. As permanent damage is inflicted, water starts leaking out more often and your Nimbus spreads farther. And because the AI will be busy compensating for the faulty pipes system, when you want to minimize the effects of bugs in the blueprint (Paradox), it won't have as much free processing power to dedicate. So if you remove the soul, its just means you don't have the AI to run your programs. When you replace the soul, the new one will still be damaged, because the same awful pipe system will still be in place.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Observation:</b></i> After re-reading it, this explanation sounds very Free Council to me. By this metaphor, Mind is the compiler that optimizes the blueprint via yantras and a Legacy is a custom programming library.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-10-2018, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T10:59:29-07:00","id":1245141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1244616-spells-that-affect-wisdom-in-game-explanation-of-why-they-re-impossible?p=1244636#post1244636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe you could replace 'soul' with 'gnosis' in that explanation. Sophia and Gnosis could be two aspects of the same thing: the Gnosis is the strength of connection to the Supernal, whilst Sophia is the stability of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me wonder if there is &quot;Sophia&quot; in a mage's Oneiros, representing his Wisdom. And if so, would she be an aspect of a Daimon, or a separate entity? The same could be asked about Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T19:12:53-07:00","id":1245284,"title":"","content":"Ima quote myself:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169733-what-is-the-cause-of-wisdom?p=1171591#post1171591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In-universe, it's easiest to think of Wisdom less as a measure of a Mage's actions and more as a measure of how healthy their soul is. A Mage's soul is a vessel bursting with Truth, a Truth that impresses itself upon reality without particular thought or care. To cast a spell is to unleash that Truth, to claim privilege and impose preference. But oftentimes, especially when young, a Mage does not want to do this willy-nilly. There are still Sleeper concerns they care about. They have priorities in life other than the discovery of another Supernal nuance. For these Mages, the health of their soul is important, because that's what gives them the capacity to choose between those concerns and chasing their Obsessions.<br /> <br /> Wisdom is the principles and practices, the code of thought and behavior, that are recognized to maintain the health of a Mage's soul. Mainly, it is noticed that people who don't follow them are well-correlated with people who have damaged souls, who bleed their Truth into the world. It's not entirely clear what the mechanism between these two things are, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, what 21C Hermit said: you can if you're an Archmaster, because Wisdom is on the same level of Mystery as an Awakening. Without crossing that line, a normal Mage just doesn't have quite enough punch.<br /> <br /> Imagine a spell with which you could optimize all of your spellcasting according to a number of parameters. What would it take to cast that spell? It's a theoretically possible spell.<br /> <br /> There exists in fiction (that I won't divulge publicly, because I feel it's a spoiler) a woman who has the superpower of &quot;seeing the path to victory&quot;. She doesn't have superstrength or hyperintelligence: she just knows exactly what must be done in order to win. Could you cast a spell to have that power? To know with certainty that if you cast this spell with these Arcana, these modifiers, at this opponent, then the Paradox will rebound exactly correctly to hurt precisely who you want hurt? It's a theoretically possible spell.<br /> <br /> Wisdom is a little bit like Gross Dosmestic Product. Could you cast a spell to end an economic depression? To, say, fix the housing bubble of 2010? I think so, but what exactly would it take to be successful? Archmastery, at least, I'd say. That's the kind of spell on the same level as &quot;rewriting the past&quot; that Archmastery games are said to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T20:25:46-07:00","id":1245301,"title":"","content":"Oh, that makes a ton of sense - a mage can't turn supernal truth against itself. Supernal truth drives mages toward Madness, not away from it. That Truth won't betray itself by working to bolster Wisdom -- those two forces oppose one another. May as well try to use magic to strengthen the Lie.<br /> <br /> That's a very succinct and straight-forward in-universe explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T21:00:06-07:00","id":1245312,"title":"","content":"...So as an aside, how do Ephemerals with the Wisdom Influence work? So they only work on lesser wisdom, or can a Rank 5 spirit potentially grant a dot under certain circumstances (and a ton of Essence)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T22:57:53-07:00","id":1245342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1244616-spells-that-affect-wisdom-in-game-explanation-of-why-they-re-impossible?p=1245312#post1245312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...So as an aside, how do Ephemerals with the Wisdom Influence work? So they only work on lesser wisdom, or can a Rank 5 spirit potentially grant a dot under certain circumstances (and a ton of Essence)?</div> </div> </div> </div>They affect lesser wisdom since they're not Supernal. Abyssal entities can apparently drop Wisdom temporarily with some of their powers though, probably inflicting Conditions along the way that can run the risk of permanently lowering your Wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}